    <div class="page">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 23 August 2026</p>

      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Andorra Private (“we”, “us” or “our”) collects, uses and protects your personal data when you visit privateandorra.com or submit information through our forms.</p>

      <p>We process personal data in accordance with the <strong>Llei 29/2021, del 28 d’octubre, qualificada de protecció de dades personals</strong> of the Principality of Andorra (LQPD) and related regulations.</p>

      <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
      <p>The data controller is the operator of privateandorra.com.</p>
      <p>For any privacy-related enquiry, please contact us at:<br>
      <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a></p>

      <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect the following personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address (when you submit an interest form)</li>
        <li>Technical data such as IP address, browser type and basic usage data (collected automatically for security and analytics purposes)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <p>We process your data for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Responding to your interest</strong> in residency or property opportunities in Andorra — based on your consent (Art. 6.1.a LQPD)</li>
        <li><strong>Improving the website and ensuring security</strong> — based on our legitimate interest (Art. 6.1.f LQPD)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We use the following service providers who may process data on our behalf:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — for form submissions</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — for website hosting</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These providers act as data processors and are required to protect your data under appropriate agreements.</p>
      <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>

      <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
      <p>We keep your email address only for as long as necessary to respond to your enquiry or until you ask us to delete it. Technical logs are retained for a limited period for security purposes.</p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under Andorran law (LQPD) you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access your personal data</li>
        <li>Rectify inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Request erasure of your data</li>
        <li>Restrict or object to processing</li>
        <li>Data portability (where applicable)</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>7. Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you believe your data protection rights have been infringed, you may lodge a complaint with the <strong>Agència Andorrana de Protecció de Dades (APDA)</strong>:</p>
      <p>
        C/ Dr. Vilanova, 15-17<br>
        AD500 Andorra la Vella<br>
        Principality of Andorra<br>
        <a href="https://www.apda.ad" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.apda.ad</a>
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version will always be published on this page.</p>
